{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1387536-consilii","id":1387536,"title":"Consilii","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-11T10:24:36-07:00","id":1387536,"title":"Consilii","content":"I'm new to Awakening. I have played and ST oWoD for years. So I am familiar with the system, familiar with Ascension. With that being said, I am wanting to run a Awakening game. I am setting the game in the Dallas/Ft Worth metroplex. I am wanting Dallas to be Pentacle territory and Ft. Worth to be Seers territory. Now to the point of me posting.....I would like some examples of Consilii....in your game, what's the structure of the Consilium? Did you go 'traditional' or did you completely homebrewed yours? What makes yours different? Do you have a large population in your Consilium? Or is it just a few Mages? Is there a published Seers Tetrarchy that's the &quot;ruling force&quot; of a city? If not, has any of you all had a Seers being the major power of a setting? Hoping to get a idea how I want to build my setting so any and all feed back will be much appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T12:12:29-07:00","id":1387564,"title":"","content":"It all depends on the size of the city, the type of story you want to tell and how many NPCs you are comfortable with managing at once.<br /> <br /> You can find an example of a Consilium here:<br /> <a href=\"https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2016/11/mage-awakening-2nd-ed-san-diego.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2016/1...san-diego.html</a><br /> <br /> Here is a sample of some simple adaptations of the Lex Magicka to the Consilium's needs here:<br /> <a href=\"https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2016/11/mage-awakening-2nd-ed-lex-magica-of-san.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2016/1...ca-of-san.html</a><br /> <br /> This shows how the city's history and themes were fleshed out:<br /> <a href=\"https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2016/11/mage-awakening-2nd-edition-mystical.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2016/1...-mystical.html</a><br /> <br /> Finally,here you can find an example of a Seer cabal:<br /> <a href=\"https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2017/07/mage-2-dethroned-queen-pylon-votaries.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2017/0...-votaries.html</a><br /> <br /> There are all sorts of useful articles there, but I think those are the most closely related to what you are looking for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T12:33:25-07:00","id":1387568,"title":"","content":"Those sound like good references. Except for the Seers. I am wanting more then just one Pylon. I am wanting a Tetrarchy....a Seers Consilium. In a Tetrarchy, is there different Ministries or does a Tetrarchy compose of only one Ministry? And if multiple Ministries in a Tetrarchy, how bad is the back stabbing, double dealing and cut throating? And on the flip side of the Tetrarchy, how would the Sleeper society be affected? And, frankly, has there been a city....metropolis .... majority under the heel of a Tetrarchy? And if so what if Pentacle mages in the area?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T19:45:20-07:00","id":1387632,"title":"","content":"Backstabbing is the name of the game for the Seers. If your superior gives you something, its probably because they expect something in return. They will use you for everything you are worth. If you are not skilled, you will meet a horrible end, but they figure its better you than them.<br /> <br /> If you are skilled, you need to remain useful or they will eliminate you once you have a chance to become a rival. Which is sensible, because Klingon Promotions abound. Cabals have comrades, Pylons have allies of convenience that can and will backstab you for their personal advancement, or just to settle a grudge. Once you become a Seer, you can never truly trust anyone again.<br /> <br /> Joining them may also happen due to blackmail or other forms of coercion. At one point you realize you are too deep to ever get out.<br /> <br /> Cities can have multiple Ministries, all working at different angles to make Sleepers exist in sustained suffering. Your privileges are based on delivering an exquisite crop of misery to the Exarch. It must be abundant, refined and arrive in a timely manner.<br /> <br /> In the end, Ministries also compete with others for dominance of a city, even those dedicated to the same Exarch. Since there is only so much prestige to go around, they need less competition.<br /> <br /> The things that make multiple Ministries work as one are either an exceptional leader or the Exarchs themselves having such a big emergency that they force them to cooperate. But given that its not the norm, they often make for less cohesive groups.<br /> <br /> How they interact with the Pentacle differs in each city, but when their numbers are about even, the default is Cold War styled peace, secured by the possibility of mutually assured annihilation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-11-2020, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T20:20:14-07:00","id":1387638,"title":"","content":"Thanx KaiserAfini. The info about the Seers is what I was curious bout. With light of this info, I am going to have to have at least 3 Ministries in the setting. I was already wanting a &quot;Cold War&quot; approach. Since I am going to be using Dallas/Ft.Worth as my setting and already decided that Dallas is Pentacle territory and Ft. Worth will be Seers territory. Arlington is going to be a &quot;neutral ground&quot; where the &quot;cold war&quot; is going to be played out. And to add a deeper layer to the setting I am thinking bout having Arlington be Changeling territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T21:04:59-07:00","id":1387641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahjemm01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1387536-consilii?p=1387638#post1387638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanx KaiserAfini. The info about the Seers is what I was curious bout. With light of this info, I am going to have to have at least 3 Ministries in the setting. I was already wanting a &amp;quot;Cold War&amp;quot; approach. Since I am going to be using Dallas/Ft.Worth as my setting and already decided that Dallas is Pentacle territory and Ft. Worth will be Seers territory. Arlington is going to be a &amp;quot;neutral ground&amp;quot; where the &amp;quot;cold war&amp;quot; is going to be played out. And to add a deeper layer to the setting I am thinking bout having Arlington be Changeling territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to help. I also recommend the Seers book, its expands on them really well. <br /> <br /> For a Cold War approach, I think you might enjoy some Conspiracies run by the Seers:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/864775-heirs-of-the-lie-also-known-as-project-o-x-sum-up-post\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/864775-heirs-of-the-lie-also-known-as-project-o-x-sum-up-post\"> Heirs of the Lie [also known as Project O-X, sum up post] - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/864775-heirs-of-the-lie-also-known-as-project-o-x-sum-up-post\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/864775-heirs-of-the-lie-also-known-as-project-o-x-sum-up-post </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> It has all started with Imperial Mysteries. Long time ago, when the book just came out, it created a huge buzz in the forums- the concept of template evolution, </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T08:26:26-07:00","id":1387729,"title":"","content":"Regarding Seer motivations/actions/plot-drivers:<br /> <br /> Seers have strong parallels to vampires; VtM Tremere seem to be the direct inspiration. Generally, &quot;What would the Camarilla do?&quot; is a pretty good proxy for &quot;What would the Seers do?&quot; if you're more familiar with VtM.<br /> <br /> They're not creating misery fire-at-will style. They act for three reasons: (1) Because they believe an Exarch told them or one of their superiors to do something (i.e. Storyteller fiat), or (2) it provides additional control over Sleepers, or (3) to overcome an internal rivalry within the Seers.<br /> <br /> Broadly the Exarchs want to dominate Sleepers utterly until they're reduced to cattle and control Awakenings to be able to harvest new mages from that herd when needed (see the parallel to Vampire?) The Seers generally oppose Sleepers exhibiting self-determination, innovation, privacy, peaceful coexistence/tolerance, courage, unpredictability, etc...<br /> <br /> In Cold War style settings, Seers might:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Engage in proxy wars against Diamond Order mages over Sleeper organizations that are rising above the control of the Exarchs. For example, a technology company that empowers users while zealously safeguarding their privacy can be a flashpoint for a proxy war between the Seers and the Free Council.</li> <li>Seek to control and penetrate mysteries that align with or oppose the broad goals of the Exarchs, e.g. a neighborhood where all the residents seem supernaturally docile or rebellious.</li> <li>Attempt to interfere in Awakenings to provoke Tyrannic Metamorphoses to swell their numbers.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T09:29:32-07:00","id":1388065,"title":"","content":"I am familiar with VtM and the Camarilla. Now that you point that out, I am actually surprised I didn't see the similarities. That is good food for thought and definitely helps form a foundation. <br /> <br /> Another problem I am having a problem developing is a Mystery &quot;grand&quot; enough to form a Consilium around. I have gotten the idea that I want the assassination of JFK to play a big part of a Mystery. My undeveloped and just a notion for now, is that the assassination of JFK has somehow tore a &quot;hole&quot; in the Fallen World and that the Lower Depths have something to do with it...or on the other side of the &quot;hole&quot;....not sure if that's a Mage like concept....but basically my thinking is that the backlash from a nation shocked, stunned, and the depression unleashed at the moment the assassination happened focused on Dealey Plaza is the cause of the &quot;hole&quot;....any suggestions, ideas, or feed back on that would also be great and appreciated","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T09:49:19-07:00","id":1388069,"title":"","content":"The easiest way to make a Mystery for a setting is to think of the &quot;rules&quot; by which Mage operates and then break however many you need to in order to make it work. A portal to a Lower Depth is perfectly appropriate. What arcana is it most closely related to? Can you think of different ways it could be exploited, protected, or guarded against? That question is particularly important since that's probably why Mages are showing up to investigate it in the first place which will help your players figure out a motivation to engage with the setting and help you round out your cast of NPCs. How does it manifest? What are the denizens like? How easy is it for stuff to come out? How has the Mystery's presence affected the way Mages structure their bits of society? Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T10:34:23-07:00","id":1388085,"title":"","content":"The way mage society would be shaped around it is going to take some thinking. And as for which Arcana....thinking several will be. My concept as of right now is that the &quot;hole&quot; has a &quot;rotating destination.&quot; That it opens up to several Realms in a cycle. And I toying with the idea that at part of the cycle is goes PAST the Lower Depths....into a alternate world...alternate Earth. A Earth with different &quot;rules&quot; of magic. This alternate Earth is actually the Earth of Ascension. Like I said....toying with the concept and just brainstorming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T10:48:33-07:00","id":1388090,"title":"","content":"Another option is to redimension how the Arcana express themselves and how the Lower Depth's hunger manifests. I think the gameplay of The Void could be a solid starting point to do this. The energy is mana, the colors are the Arcana and beings pf the Fallen World exist in its version of Twilight. You can find more info here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/XzS6RwXC-eI\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/XzS6RwXC-eI\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/XzS6RwXC-eI\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/XzS6RwXC-eI </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Its a bit long, but does an excellent job of breaking down the reasons and symbolism behind the design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T14:55:53-07:00","id":1388162,"title":"","content":"The JFK example you picked fits both DtD and MtAw just fine. (It is fairly similar to one of the example settings in DtD: Splintered City Seattle)<br /> <br /> In a Mage game, you could pull the &quot;it's an inexplicable GM plot&quot; if you really wanted to, but I suggest not. Perhaps it <i>is</i> involved, but entirely opportunistic. It saw the tear and understood how to capitalize on the strange phenomenon with some powerful new Infrastructure... unique and helpful new infrastructure, in fact. The cause of the fracture(s) could be a deeper mystery, still.<br /> <br /> Maybe some cult tried to free their dark god. This could be the cause, but it could, alternately, happen after the wheels were already in motion and be a red herring, too.<br /> <br /> Maybe a group was trying to sacrifice the &quot;king&quot; to solve the Cold War and establish decades of plenty. That the reaction of the people was so powerful might have been a miscalculation or a side effect intended only by some alternate faction.<br /> <br /> Perhaps JFK was destined to become an archmage and someone attempted to create a parallel world in which he never came to power. This would have your game (and our world) sit on that side of the fence. Arch Kennedy is now unable to travel into this timeline due to that very successful Imperium Rite.<br /> <br /> The pain created a wound, exactly as the tempters intended, and now they have a freer hand in manipulating world politics. Maybe the demons are setting up the destruction of the world primarily to create a bargaining chip to persuade some individuals to behave in a way that suits them. <br /> <br /> <br /> You can work out different tiers involved at various levels and make this run in a number of directions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T15:38:45-07:00","id":1388168,"title":"","content":"Well idk anything bout DTD. Lol. Thenate's post has inspired me. That inspiration has me now toying with the idea that it was a Imperial Ritual with the intention that JFK was the subject of a powerful Fate/Prime/Time Ritual with the intention that the Cold War would be ended, peace was Fated to develop, and the Space program was going to usher in huge break in the Lie and Sleepers knowing more of the Supernal. But the God Machine had other plans and the Exarch's agreed with those ideas of the God Machine, and assassinated JFK. The clash of Imperial Power BROKE the God Machine in the vicinity Dealey Plaza. The God Machine is still attempting to repair the massive blacklash of the event.<br /> <br /> Oh and maybe when Contagion comes out, I can use that to show how the God Machine is broken or the lengths it's going to to fix the broken area.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","user":"Mahjemm01","date":". 05-13-2020, 06:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}